{
  "id": "scots",
  "name": "Scots",
  "abbr": "sco",
  "slug": "scots",
  "classes": "Infantry, Defense, Mustering",
  "description": "The Scots field resilient infantry that excel at ambushing enemies from stealth. Tower Houses and Keeps protect their communities and precious cattle from raiders across the countryside. Muster reinforcements quickly at the Mustering Hall and research powerful Highland or Lowland technologies and secure the Kingdom of Scotland.",
  "overview": [
    {
      "title": "Civilization Bonuses",
      "list": [
        "Ghillies can stealth in the open.",
        "Infantry have vision and movement speed bonuses while in Stealth Forests.",
        "Tower Houses replace Outposts, produce Highland Cattle, and increase population.",
        "Highland Cattle graze at Berry Bushes to gather Food over time.",
        "Highland Landmarks increase Highland Cattle capacity.",
        "Muster units quickly at the Mustering Hall from Feudal Age (II).",
        "Research powerful technologies from the Lowlands and Highlands at the Mustering Hall.",
        "Kirkmen can create Fishponds to gather Gold and increase the gather rates of nearby workers.",
        "Lowland Landmarks increase the Fishpond build limit.",
        "Destroyed Keeps can be repaired for a limited time before being completely destroyed.",
        "Destroyed Keeps create a scorched-earth effect that reduces the combat effectiveness of nearby enemies.",
        "Naval arrowslits are 50% cheaper."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Noble Houses",
      "description": "Tower Houses replace Outposts, produce Highland Cattle, Ghillies, and increase population."
    },
    {
      "title": "Highland Wealth",
      "description": "Protect Highland Cattle while they graze at Berry Bushes, providing Food over time as they eat. Cattle capacity increases with each Highland Landmark built."
    },
    {
      "title": "Highland Ambush",
      "description": "Infantry have deep knowledge and connection to their lands and fight with advantage in and around Stealth Forests. No vision penalties while in Stealth Forests and movement speed is increased when Highland Ambush is active."
    },
    {
      "title": "Scottish Schiltron",
      "description": "Gallowglass can brace for cavalry charges by default, and Men-at-Arms can brace after Lochaber Axes is researched."
    },
    {
      "title": "Lowlands and Highlands",
      "description": "Choose between a Highland or a Lowland Landmark each time when aging up. The Mustering Hall holds unique technologies from these lands. As Landmarks are constructed from a region, the associated technologies halve in cost for its support."
    },
    {
      "title": "Answer the Call",
      "description": "Muster warriors quickly at the Mustering Hall from the Feudal Age (II)."
    },
    {
      "title": "Monastic Fishponds",
      "description": "Create harvestable Fishponds with a Kirkman to gather Gold. Workers near active Fishponds receive increased gather rates. Landmarks from the Lowlands increase the maximum Fishpond count."
    },
    {
      "title": "Castle Ruins",
      "description": "Upon destruction, Keeps adopt scorched earth tactics and sabotage the immediate area for a duration. If any enemies are within the area of sabotage their combat effectiveness is temporarily reduced. During this time Keeps become Keep Ruins and can be saved from total destruction if repaired. Keep Ruins can be fully restored for up to maximum of 600 Stone after which repairing Keep Ruins becomes free."
    },
    {
      "title": "Loch Defensive Network",
      "description": "Dock defensive arrowslits are 50% cheaper."
    },
    {
      "title": "Influence",
      "description": "Construct military buildings around the Mustering Hall to increase its level to improve the efficiency of mustering warriors.\nTier 1: Unlocks mustering of Highland Archers. Adds a muster charge. \nTier 2: Reduces cost to muster. Adds a muster charge.\nTier 3: Reduces cost to muster. Adds a muster charge. Mustered warrior health is increased."
    }
  ],
